Row 1: HR advisory - Evaluated Pricing Scenario
Row 2: Proponents must price the standardized scenario. The scenario will be used for evaluation purposes only and does not represent a purchase commitment.
Row 3: Context: 
The engagement is intended to help the Bank:
•  Identify workforce trends, risks, and capability gaps that could affect future business outcomes;
•  Assess the organization's readiness to meet future talent and workforce requirements;
•  Strengthen workforce planning practices and decision-making;
•  Support succession readiness and talent sustainability for critical roles; and
•  Develop a practical roadmap to address identified workforce priorities.
•  Interviews, meetings, stakeholder engagements, workshops, and presentations will be conducted in either English or French, as required by the Bank.
Row 5: Specs - Assumptions:  
•  The engagement will be completed over approximately twelve (12) weeks;
•  Stakeholders are located within Canada;
•  All work will be conducted virtually;
•  Bank representatives will provide access to required documentation, workforce data, and stakeholders in a timely manner; and
•  One (1) consolidated round of revisions is included.
•  Provide your pricing in years 2 and 3 for delivering an identical engagement
Row 7: Specs - Discovery and assessment:
Assume:
•  Review up to twenty (20) Bank documents, including workforce data, HR reports, planning documents, and organizational information;
•  Review workforce datasets, including demographics, movement trends, vacancies, retirement eligibility, workforce planning metrics, and related indicators;
•  Conduct fifteen (15) stakeholder interviews of sixty (60) minutes each with HR and senior business leaders on workforce priorities, risks, succession, talent needs, and future capabilities; 
•  Conduct one (1) three-hour stakeholder validation session to review findings, validate observations, and discuss priority workforce planning considerations; 
• Assess current workforce planning practices, workforce risks, and workforce-related challenges;
•  Identify current and future workforce capability requirements; and
•  Develop a workforce planning assessment summarizing key findings, risks, opportunities, and observations.
Row 9: Specs - Analysis and recommendation:
Assume:
•  Analyze information gathered through document review, workforce datasets, stakeholder consultations, and other Bank-provided information;
•  Identify critical workforce risks, future workforce challenges, and priority workforce planning considerations;
•  Develop recommendations on workforce planning, talent sustainability, succession readiness, and future workforce requirements;
•  Identify implementation considerations, dependencies, assumptions, and risks; and
•  Develop a prioritized implementation roadmap.
Row 11: Specs - Reporting and executive presentation
Assume:
•  Prepare one (1) final report (English only) summarizing findings, observations, and recommendations;
•  Prepare and deliver one (1) ninety (90) minute executive presentation (English only) of findings and recommendations for the Senior Human Resources Leadership Team; and
•  Incorporate one (1) consolidated round of feedback into final deliverables.
Row 13: Specs - Program management:  
Assume three (3) hours per week of ongoing project management throughout the engagement, including:
•  Project planning and coordination;
•  Stakeholder scheduling and engagement;
•  Status reporting and progress updates;
•  Deliverables management and quality assurance; and
•  General project administration associated with the engagement.
Row 15: Exclusions:
•  Travel expenses
